Something appears at your feet
D - 3 darts named Bully's darts.

Bully's darts never disappear when thrown they way normal darts
sometimes do, and they do extra damage against all monsters. You can
#invoke them every few hundred turns to produce 2 zorkmids (your BFH).
Also, their to-hit chance is unaffected by the player's level in the
darts skill- an expert character is just as (in)accurate as an
unskilled one. However, if the first to-hit calculation fails, the game
rolls again against the character's luck (because darts matches often
seem to be more luck than judgement, especially after a few !oBooze.)

Most importantly though, Bully's darts provide useful commentary
whenever you use them, for example:

You throw 3 Blessed +4 Bully's darts --more--
The first dart hit the goblin! Super! --more--
The 2nd dart hits the goblin! The Goblin is killed! Smashing! --more--
The third dart hit the Watch Captain! The Watch Captain gets angry!
Great! --more--

Or, if a single dart takes a monster from full HP to death in a single
throw:
The dart hits the jackal! The jackal is killed! Iiiiin one!

And so on.



